CAT = "sfadminSales"; SEG = "SAL"
Q = [
('When a qualified lead is converted, which records can Salesforce create from it?',
 'Account, contact and opportunity', ['Case, contact and task', 'Account, campaign and quote', 'Contract, order and contact'],
 'Lead conversion creates or updates an account and a contact, and can optionally create an opportunity.'),
('A custom lead field must carry over to the contact on conversion. What should the admin set up?',
 'Lead field mapping', ['A duplicate rule on Contact', 'A lookup filter', 'A campaign member status'],
 'Custom lead fields are mapped to custom account, contact or opportunity fields in Map Lead Fields so their values carry over on conversion.'),
('How many lead assignment rules can be active at a time?',
 'One', ['Two', 'One per queue', 'No limit'],
 'Only one lead assignment rule can be active; it holds ordered rule entries that route leads to users or queues.'),
('A lead matches entries 2 and 4 of the active assignment rule. Where does it go?',
 'To the owner in entry 2', ['To the owner in entry 4', 'To both owners', 'To the default lead owner'],
 'Rule entries are checked in order and the first one that matches decides the assignment.'),
('Visitors fill in a form on the company website and should appear in Salesforce as leads. Which feature fits?',
 'Web-to-Lead', ['Email-to-Case', 'Data Loader', 'Einstein Activity Capture'],
 'Web-to-Lead generates an HTML form that creates a lead record each time it is submitted.'),
('Website leads should get an automatic thank-you email that depends on the product they chose. What should the admin use?',
 'A lead auto-response rule', ['A lead assignment rule', 'A duplicate rule on leads', 'A campaign hierarchy for products'],
 'Lead auto-response rules send a chosen email template to web leads based on criteria, such as the product of interest.'),
('Marketing wants to see revenue from all events under one annual conference. What should the admin set up?',
 'A campaign hierarchy', ['A record type for each event', 'A lead queue per event', 'A price book for the conference'],
 'Campaign hierarchies roll up members, responses and won opportunity values from child campaigns to their parents.'),
("Which campaign member status setting counts a person toward the campaign's responses?",
 'Responded', ['Default', 'Sent', 'Converted'],
 'Each campaign member status can be marked Responded; members with such a status are counted as responses in campaign statistics.'),
('An opportunity moves to the Closed Won stage. What else does Salesforce update from that stage?',
 'Probability and forecast category', ['The account owner and team', 'The price book on the deal', 'The campaign member status'],
 'Each opportunity stage carries a default probability and forecast category, which update when the stage changes.'),
('A product must be added to a custom price book. What must exist first?',
 'A standard price for it', ['A quote on an opportunity', 'A product schedule', 'An active campaign'],
 'A product needs an entry in the standard price book before it can be given a price in any custom price book.'),
('A subscription is billed monthly over a year and sales wants that spread on the opportunity product. Which feature does this?',
 'Revenue schedules', ['Price book entries', 'Opportunity splits', 'Campaign influence'],
 "Revenue (and quantity) schedules divide an opportunity product's amount or quantity into installments over time."),
('An opportunity has three quotes. How many can be synced with the opportunity at once?',
 'One', ['Two', 'All three', 'None, quotes never sync'],
 'Only one quote can sync with an opportunity at a time; syncing keeps its line items and the opportunity products the same.'),
('Two reps worked a deal and should share credit for its amount. Which feature fits?',
 'Opportunity splits', ['Opportunity teams only', 'Revenue schedules', 'Account teams'],
 'Opportunity splits divide credit for an opportunity among team members; revenue splits must total 100 percent.'),
('In collaborative forecasts, whose numbers roll up to a forecast manager?',
 'Users below them in the hierarchy', ['Users in the same queue', 'Users in the same public group', 'All users with sales licenses'],
 'Forecasts roll up through the forecast hierarchy, which follows the role hierarchy, to the forecast manager of each role.'),
('A contact works with several accounts as a consultant. How can one contact record be related to them all?',
 'Contacts to Multiple Accounts', ['A second contact record for each', 'Person accounts for consultants', 'An account team on each account'],
 'Contacts to Multiple Accounts lets a contact keep a primary account and have indirect relationships to other accounts.'),
('A company sells to individual consumers and wants one record per person that acts as both account and contact. What should it use?',
 'Person accounts', ['Accounts with no contacts', 'Leads only', 'Contacts with no accounts'],
 'Person accounts combine account and contact fields for individuals. Once enabled they cannot be turned off.'),
('A parent company and its subsidiaries should appear as a tree on the account. Which field builds this?',
 'Parent Account', ['Account Owner', 'Account Site', 'Reports To'],
 'Linking accounts through the Parent Account field builds an account hierarchy that users can view.'),
("Accounts in each sales region should be assigned to that region's reps automatically by postcode and industry. Which feature fits?",
 'Enterprise Territory Management', ['Opportunity splits by region', 'A campaign hierarchy by region', 'Lead auto-response rules'],
 "Enterprise Territory Management uses territory assignment rules to assign accounts to territories, giving the territory's users access."),
('Sales leaders want an email whenever an opportunity over a set amount reaches a high probability. Which feature does this without code?',
 'Big Deal Alerts', ['Collaborative forecasts', 'Lead assignment rules', 'Revenue schedules'],
 'Opportunity (Big Deal) alerts email chosen people when an opportunity reaches the amount and probability thresholds the admin sets.'),
('A sales manager wants to add a list of event attendees from a report to a campaign in one step. What can she do?',
 'Add them as campaign members', ['Convert them all to accounts', 'Assign them to a lead queue', 'Merge them into one lead'],
 'Leads and contacts can be added to a campaign from a report or list view, or by import, becoming campaign members.'),
]
